// Instrumental  [audioEffect] — one mix in, the same record without its voice out.
//
// The SAME separation as `stemsplit`, and that is the point of extending it rather than copying it: one
// model, one inference, one place where the model's name lives. What differs is the single line below —
// the outputs. A separating pass writes what its module declares, so declaring one output named
// `instrumental` is how a chain asks for the sum of everything the voice is not.
//
// Why not sum the four files afterwards: three of them are hundreds of megabytes that would travel a
// network to be added together and thrown away. The pass already holds the parts in memory, unmixed.
extends("@st0/cold/stemsplit")
// `type` is repeated rather than inherited: a child's `plugin:` REPLACES its parent's whole block,
// so naming this one without it would leave a module nothing recognises as offline.
plugin({ type: "offline", name: "Instrumental" })
// One audio output, and its NAME is what the pass reads — `instrumental` is the only name that means
// "every stem but the voice". A stem's own name here would write that stem instead.
outputs([name("instrumental").type("audio")])
